# Naming Standards

Use short, standard names tied to the framework domain. **Max 2–3 words** per identifier.

## Functions

- Pattern: `verb_noun` or repo verbs `build_*`, `load_*`, `train_*`, `export_*`
- Good: `build_oracle`, `load_splits`, `train_solvability`, `patch_raw`
- Bad: `build_stratified_daar_train_val_test_splits`, `upsert_feature_parquet_for_missing_ids`

## Variables

- One concept per name; reuse repo terms
- Good: `oracle_df`, `split_id`, `cost_hand`, `agent_list`
- Bad: `daar_oracle_parquet_file_path`, `missing_feature_training_id_list`

## Paths & config

- D-AAR prefix: `daar_*` only under `datasets/daar/`
- Good: `daar_root`, `oracle_path`, `splits_dir`, `plans_cache`
- Bad: mixing `exp2`, `offline`, `daar` for the same artifact

## Models & artifacts

- Pattern: `{domain}_{role}`
- Good: `solvability_hgbm`, `cost_simulator`, `split_manifest`
- Bad: `daar_per_agent_solvability_classifier_model_v1`

## Constants

- `UPPER_SNAKE`, 2–3 words: `AGENT_LIST`, `SPLIT_ORDER`, `DEFAULT_SEED`

## Columns & symbols (frozen — do not rename)

- Oracle: `r_a`, `X1`, `X2`, `d`, `solvable`, `daar_split`
- Features: `dim_*`, `heur_*`, `phi_q`
- Cost: `cost_hand`, `C_static`, `X2_dynamic`

## Consistency rules

1. Pick one term — do not mix synonyms (`split` vs `partition` vs `fold`)
2. Reuse existing helpers before adding new names
3. No unused exports or duplicate path aliases
4. Match surrounding file style (imports, types, docstrings)
